{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3830,3910p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'condition-identical|saved-protocol|retain|later|clojure/protocol' test/yang/call/exception*.clj; rg -n 'reserved|check-program-symbols|check-binder|rewrite-ex-info' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"on the stack. No caller-side rewrapping or language-pair cache is allowed.\n\nThese are in-task rules. A closure, continuation, cell, or live invocation\nis not made portable by this convention. Linker/UCF custody and admission\nstill govern task/host crossings; currently refused cell-bearing lifts\nremain refused. Live closures in an invocation must not be placed in\ncanonical literal data or sent as a purported portable request.\n\n#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\n\nNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\nextra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\nlanguage-specific return instruction.\n\nAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\n\n```clojure\n{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\n```\n\nThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\nordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\nLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\nmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\nthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\nsynthesized.\n\nProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\n`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\nthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\noriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\ncallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\n`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\n\nThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\n\n1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\n   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\n2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\n   may deliver the original payload directly.\n3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\n   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\ninvoke a foreign method.\n\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n\nVM application/custody defects and host implementation failures remain\noperational failures. Do not catch them broadly and relabel them as\nsource exceptions. Existing explicit stream/module refusals keep their\nsource mappings under the relevant profiles.\n\n#### 8.10.8 Cleanup, re-entry, and suspension\n\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:21:   `retain` returns normally before `later` raises from a new activation.\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:36:              \"def retain(f):\" \"    global saved\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:39:              \"def later():\" \"    raise saved\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:55:        \"globalThis.retain = function(f) { try { return f(); } catch (e) { saved = e; return e; } };\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:56:        \"globalThis.later = function() { throw saved; };\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:66:        \"function retain($f) { global $saved; try { return $f(); } catch (Throwable $e) { $saved = $e; return $e; } }\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:67:        \"function later() { global $saved; throw $saved; }\"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:78:        \"(defn retain [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (cell/set! saved e) e))) \"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:79:        \"(defn later [] (throw (cell/get saved))) \"\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:113:                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:122:        (fixture :retained-foreign-lifetime f #{::r2 ::r5}\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:123:                 {:retained true :local-foreign-exception true\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:125:                  :condition-identical true :payload-identical true}))\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:127:        (fixture (keyword (str \"saved-protocol-\" (name reason))) f #{::r3 ::r5}\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:128:                 {:retained true :transferred true :once true :after false\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:129:                  :condition-identical true :reason reason}\ntest/yang/call/exception_contract.clj:153:   :retained-lifetime #{::r1 ::r2}\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:124:           :retained-lifetime\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:178:        :retained-lifetime\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:184:                (assoc transfer :retained (list '= :return (list 'get 'leg.saved :route))\ntest/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:203:      (= scenario :retained-lifetime) (assoc :retained true :local true))))\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:72:        retained 'probe.retained\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:79:                                :condition-identical\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:114:              (if (.startsWith (name scenario) \"saved-protocol-\")\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:115:                (list 'let [retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:116:                            result (call (export \"later\") [])]\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:119:                               :retained (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return))))\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:129:                    result (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])]\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:134:        (#{:foreign-reception :retained-foreign-lifetime} scenario)\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:141:                    retained (call (export \"retain\") ['probe.injected])\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:142:                    wrapper (list 'get retained :value)\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:143:                    'probe.local (list 'if (list '= :return (list 'get retained :route))\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:147:                    returned (list '= (list 'get retained :route) :return)]\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:151:                  (list 'let [result (call (export \"later\") [])]\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:154:                                 :retained returned :local-foreign-exception local\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:155:                                 :condition-identical (list '= condition (list 'get result :condition))\ntest/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:180:   must finish retain before entering later. `run-fixture` remains available\n52:;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n63:  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of contract C1.\"\n388:;; Generated names carry the reserved `dsg__` prefix and derive from the\n410:(def ^:private reserved-prefix \"dsg__\")\n418:(defn- reserved-name?\n420:  (= reserved-prefix (subs (name sym) 0 (min (count (name sym))\n421:                                             (count reserved-prefix)))))\n425:  \"A definition name is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix.\"\n429:  (when (reserved-name? sym)\n430:    (reject! \"Definition name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n431:             {:name sym, :prefix reserved-prefix})))\n434:(defn- check-binder!\n440:    (when (reserved-name? b)\n441:      (reject! \"Binding name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n442:               {:binder b, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n463:              (check-binder! (second xs) pattern)\n469:            (check-binder! sym pattern)\n478:              (check-binder! x pattern)\n508:  (cond-> (symbol (str reserved-prefix path))\n554:          (do (check-binder! target target)\n567:          :else (check-binder! target target))))))\n579:            (check-binder! p params)\n672:  \"Every macro parameter is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix; an\n676:    (check-binder! p params)\n803:(def ^:private av-sym (symbol (