{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '478,497p' src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc; rg -n 'defn content=|closure|Closure' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | head -45; git diff --name-only 8cd9fc92..778747ce; git show 778747ce:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | nl -ba | sed -n '2540,2609p'; sed -n '1300,1410p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- ref?\n  \"True when `x` is a stream, cursor or cell reference.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (contains? #{:stream-ref :cursor-ref :cell-ref} (:type x))))\n\n\n(defn- data-content=\n  \"True when `a` and `b` have one identity under content addressing:\n   Jing's kind-strict content equality, so every NaN is one value, 0.0 is\n   not -0.0, 1 is not 1.0, and collections recurse. A callable or a\n   reference compares by host `=`, so content addressing never walks it.\"\n  [a b]\n  (or (identical? a b)\n      (if (or (callable? a) (callable? b) (ref? a) (ref? b))\n        (= a b)\n        (cbor/content= a b))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module\n561:(defn content=\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-x1aAtbBl' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-11 03:14:47.677 xcodebuild[97187:121021459]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-11 03:14:47.904 xcodebuild[97187:121021430] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-6qExmkPl' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-11 03:14:48.661 xcodebuild[97193:121021526]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-11 03:14:48.873 xcodebuild[97193:121021524] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-kBxu4dLD' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-11 03:14:50.409 xcodebuild[97216:121021581]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-11 03:14:50.576 xcodebuild[97216:121021580] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-DSbbpV4D' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-11 03:14:51.248 xcodebuild[97221:121021627]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-11 03:14:51.443 xcodebuild[97221:121021625] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n  2540\t                                      ;; any `:id` spelling may be asked\n  2541\t                                      ;; about and the r4 heap-id-language\n  2542\t                                      ;; discriminator is retired. A shape\n  2543\t                                      ;; the heap does not authenticate is\n  2544\t                                      ;; data: it falls to the witness\n  2545\t                                      ;; branch and, entryless, is no more\n  2546\t                                      ;; admitted than any other source map,\n  2547\t                                      ;; so its invocation stays ordinary\n  2548\t                                      ;; map data. An authenticated\n  2549\t                                      ;; reference dereferences; an\n  2550\t                                      ;; authenticated cell whose contents\n  2551\t                                      ;; carry no callable entry is not\n  2552\t                                      ;; admitted (authentication is not\n  2553\t                                      ;; authorization, rule 3), and the\n  2554\t                                      ;; call-site routing that consulted\n  2555\t                                      ;; here refuses it as not-callable.\n  2556\t                                      (let [dsg__cell-ref?\n  2557\t                                            (if (dsg__equal\n  2558\t                                                  (dsg__get dsg__candidate :type)\n  2559\t                                                  :cell-ref)\n  2560\t                                              (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n  2561\t                                                                  :id)\n  2562\t                                                (if (data/contains? dsg__candidate\n  2563\t                                                                    :seal)\n  2564\t                                                  (if (dsg__equal\n  2565\t                                                        (data/count dsg__candidate)\n  2566\t                                                        3)\n  2567\t                                                    (if (data/string?\n  2568\t                                                          (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n  2569\t                                                                    :seal))\n  2570\t                                                      (if (dsg__equal\n  2571\t                                                            (data/str-length\n  2572\t                                                              (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n  2573\t                                                                        :seal))\n  2574\t                                                            64)\n  2575\t                                                        true\n  2576\t                                                        false)\n  2577\t                                                      false)\n  2578\t                                                    false)\n  2579\t                                                  false)\n  2580\t                                                false)\n  2581\t                                              false)]\n  2582\t                                        (if dsg__cell-ref?\n  2583\t                                          (if (cell/authentic? dsg__candidate)\n  2584\t                                            (let [dsg__descriptor\n  2585\t                                                  (cell/get dsg__candidate)\n  2586\t                                                  dsg__entry\n  2587\t                                                  (dsg__get dsg__descriptor\n  2588\t                                                            :yang.call/entry)]\n  2589\t                                              (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n  2590\t                                            false)\n  2591\t                                          (let [dsg__entry\n  2592\t                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n  2593\t                                                          :yang.call/entry)\n  2594\t                                                dsg__witness\n  2595\t                                                (dsg__get dsg__candidate\n  2596\t                                                          :clj/admission)]\n  2597\t                                            (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n  2598\t                                              (if (data/callable? dsg__witness)\n  2599\t                                                (dsg__equal\n  2600\t                                                  dsg__witness\n  2601\t                                                  (dsg__make_admission\n  2602\t                                                    (dsg__assoc dsg__candidate\n  2603\t                                                                :clj/admission\n  2604\t                                                                nil)))\n  2605\t                                                false)\n  2606\t                                              false))))\n  2607\t                                      false)))\n  2608\t                               ;; The intra-unit dispatcher: resolve the unit's public entry,\n  2609\t                               ;; apply it with the compiler's token packet [token args] - one\n             (run-outcome [(list 'let [binding 5]\n                                 '(let [f (fn [x] x)] (f 21)))]))))\n    (testing (str \"a later source definition of \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok 21]\n             (run-outcome [(list 'def binding 5) '(defn f\n                                                    [x]\n                                                    x) '(f 21)]))))\n    (testing (str \"raise through a parameter named \" binding)\n      (is (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"boom\", :yin.k/data {:x 21}}]\n             (run-outcome\n               ['(defn g\n                   []\n                   (throw (ex-info \"boom\" {:x 21})))\n                (list 'defn 'f [binding] '(g))\n                '(+ 1 (f 5))])))))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok 1]\n         (run-outcome '[(def f (let [get 5] (fn [x] x))) (f 1)]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-source-admission\n  (doseq [form '[(let [x 5] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:ordinary :map}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry 5}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:py/type :function :code :legacy}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry 5}] ((if true x x) 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)}] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc {} :yang.call/entry (get f :yang.call/entry))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc f :extra :forged)] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc f :yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry g))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x (assoc {} :yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)\n                                :clj/admission (get f :clj/admission))] (x 1))\n                 (let [x {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)\n                          :clj/admission (fn [x] true)}] (x 1))]]\n    (doseq [wrap [identity #(list '+ 1 %)]]\n      (let [result (run-outcome ['(defn f\n                                    [x]\n                                    x)\n                                 '(defn g\n                                    [x]\n                                    (+ x 1)) (wrap form)])]\n        (is (= :yin.k/error (first result)) (pr-str form))\n        (is (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason (second result)))\n            (pr-str form)))))\n  (is (= [:yin.k/ok [false false true 21]]\n         (run-outcome '[(defn f\n                          [x]\n                          x)\n                        [(yang.call/eligible? {:yang.call/entry (yang.call/entry f)})\n                         (yang.call/eligible? (assoc f :extra :forged))\n                         (yang.call/eligible? f)\n                         (f 21)]]))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-token-packet-forgery-refuses\n  (testing \"a forged vector applied to the extracted public entry never\n            enters the private body: the entry authenticates the packet on\n            the compiler-held token and forged shapes refuse. The extraction\n            and application happen INSIDE a compiled program (the packet\n            dispatch lives in its preamble scope), the call spliced in as\n            UAST over a marker call, on both evaluators.\"\n    ;; forged VECTORS are the packet-dispatch axis (the P1 axis): each must\n    ;; produce an error outcome without the body running. Scalar and empty\n    ;; invocations hit the public entry's pre-existing non-record refusal\n    ;; (a host throw, same before D2) and are covered by the entry's own\n    ;; behavior, not this regression.\n    (doseq [forged '[[] [42] [nil [42]] [a b c d]]]\n      (let [;; the packet dispatch reached at runtime: extract the public\n            ;; entry of the target (a source defn), then apply the forged\n            ;; vector to it directly - bypassing source lowering entirely\n            call-ast (u/let1 'raw\n                             (u/app (u/v 'yang.call/entry) (u/v 'target))\n                             (u/app (u/v 'raw) (u/lit forged)))\n            ast (walk/postwalk\n                  (fn [node]\n                    (if (= node (u/v 'marker-call)) call-ast node))\n                  (yang/compile-program\n                    ['(defn target\n                        [x]\n                        :private-body-entered)\n                     '(marker-call)]\n                    true\n                    {:convention :arg-vector\n                     :outcomes true\n                     :native (set (keys vm/primitive-profiles))}))]\n        (doseq [run [walker-run semantic-run]]\n          (let [result (try\n                         (first (run ast))\n                         (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n                           (pr-str {:caught (ex-message e) :data (ex-data e)})))]\n            (is (and (vector? result) (= :yin.k/error (first result)))\n                (str \"forged \" (pr-str forged) \" must produce an error outcome, got \"\n                     (pr-str result)))\n            ;; The sentinel must appear NOWHERE in the outcome. The codex\n            ;; mutation gate (2026-11-04) showed the previous top-level\n            ;; (not= sentinel (second result)) check passing vacuously: with\n            ;; the token check disabled the body runs and its return value\n            ;; nests inside a not-callable error payload, so the outer error\n            ;; tag satisfies assertion 1 and (second result) is the error\n            ;; map, not the sentinel. A whole-outcome traversal fails under\n            ;; that mutation and passes only when the body never ran.\n            (is (not (some #{:private-body-entered}\n                           (tree-seq coll? seq result)))\n                (str \"forged \" (pr-str forged) \" reached the body; the sentinel nests in the outcome: \"\n                     (pr-str result)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-common-call-invalid-continuation-refuses\n  (let [tamper (fn [forms]\n                 (walk/postwalk\n                   (fn [node]\n                     (if (= node u/capture) (u/lit :invalid-continuation) node))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
